    <item>
      <title>ErgoDox Split Ergonomic Keyboard Review</title>
      <link>https://andreaazzola.com/post/ergodox-ergonomic-keyboard-review/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 09 Dec 2014 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://andreaazzola.com/post/ergodox-ergonomic-keyboard-review/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://andreaazzola.com/images/ergodox_side-1.jpg&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://andreaazzola.com/images/ergodox_front-1.jpg&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://andreaazzola.com/images/ergodox_aerial-1.jpg&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;ErgoDox&lt;/strong&gt; is a DIY ergonomic keyboard, featuring a &lt;em&gt;split design&lt;/em&gt;—each half, one hand. The two halves are connected with a &lt;em&gt;phone TRRS connector cable&lt;/em&gt;, while the connection to the PC—or Mac or Unix—is obtained through a detachable mini USB.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;history&#34;&gt;History&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The project &lt;a href=&#34;https://geekhack.org/index.php?topic=22780.0&#34;&gt;has been initiated&lt;/a&gt; by Dominic Beauchamp—aka Dox, from which the keyboard name derives—on the GeekHack.org forum; the design has been largely inspired by the &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.key64.org/&#34;&gt;Key64&lt;/a&gt; project by Nestor Diaz.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
